(search_orders calls the same order-list endpoint and returns compact LLM-friendly records.) Tj T*
(get_order_by_id calls the internal-ID endpoint and preserves the raw response. get_order) Tj T*
(strips a leading # from a display reference, searches the order list, then retrieves detail by) Tj T*
(returned internal ID. get_orders_summary summarizes the retrieved page with counts,) Tj T*
(status/payment breakdowns, order value, average order value, pagination, and recent orders.) Tj T*
(get_order_stats and get_status_transitions directly wrap their confirmed endpoints.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Customers) Tj T*
(There is no dedicated customer API. find_customer and get_customer_context reuse GET) Tj T*
(/commerce/orders. Name, email, phone, and customer ID are passed through existing order) Tj T*
(search/filter behavior. Results are deduplicated by customer ID/contact/name. Multiple) Tj T*
(candidates are returned rather than silently selecting one. Context includes customer contact) Tj T*
(data, order history, purchased-item summaries, status counts, and returned order value.) Tj T*
(Limitations are inherited from order search and pagination; standalone customer statistics are) Tj T*
(not confirmed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Products and inventory) Tj T*
(get_products is the legacy/raw catalog query. Filters are SKU, name, status, barcode, brand,) Tj T*
(category, channel, vendor, seller, and warehouse. search_products returns compact results and) Tj T*
(can retrieve by product ID. get_product returns compact detail; get_product_by_id preserves) Tj T*
(raw detail. get_product_summary wraps the product summary endpoint.) Tj T*
(There is no dedicated inventory endpoint. search_inventory reads inventory or stocks attached) Tj T*
(to product records. get_inventory_summary returns the backend product summary. The MCP never) Tj T*
(assumes available stock equals on-hand minus reserved. If inventory fields are absent,) Tj T*
(inventory_available is false and the value is unavailable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Shipments and fulfillment) Tj T*
(No dedicated shipment API is implemented. search_shipments and get_order_shipments derive) Tj T*
(stored shipment data from order records, including shipments, warehouse, order status, and) Tj T*
(channel status. Tracking is stored backend data; no live carrier refresh is performed.) Tj T*
(get_fulfillment_queue uses PENDING orders and explicitly reports that separate picking/packing) Tj T*
(queue data is not exposed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. Returns and refunds) Tj T*
(No dedicated return or refund API is implemented. search_returns uses supported order statuses) Tj T*
(RETURN_REQUESTED, RETURN_RECEIVED, PARTIALLY_RETURNED, RETURNED, REFUNDED, and) Tj T*
(PARTIALLY_REFUNDED. get_order_returns searches those statuses for an order and deduplicates) Tj T*
(results. Return ID, order, customer, status, reason, timestamps, items, quantities,) Tj T*
(inspection, putaway, stock restoration, refund status, and refund amount are returned only) Tj T*
(when backend fields exist. Quantities are not locally calculated. Refund execution is not) Tj T*
(implemented. A completed/returned status does not prove a refund was paid.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(10. Business assistant) Tj T*
(get_business_summary validates an optional UTC date and composes daily orders, order) Tj T*
(statistics, and product/inventory summary. It returns as_of, period, order count, status) Tj T*
(counts, order value, successful backend sections, and safe unavailable sections. Order value) Tj T*
(is not called profit or collected cash.) Tj T*
(get_attention_queue composes pending/on-hold/partially fulfilled daily orders, pending) Tj T*
(fulfillment, pending shipment views, and returns. Each attention category includes a reason) Tj T*
(and evidence. It does not invent arbitrary priorities, live tracking, channel issues, or) Tj T*
(inventory risks that the backend cannot support. Composite calls preserve successful sections) Tj T*
(and use safe error codes for unavailable sections.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(11. Authentication flow) Tj T*
(Credential login calls POST /auth/login with email and password. Browser login uses PointNXT) Tj T*
(login URL and state-validated callback at /auth/callback; authorization code exchange also) Tj T*
ET
endstream
