(uses POST /auth/login. The authentication response supplies access token, refresh token,) Tj T*
(tenant ID, and optional user/membership/expiry values. API requests use Authorization: Bearer) Tj T*
(and x-tenant-id. A 401 triggers one refresh request. logout calls POST /auth/logout and clears) Tj T*
(the current session. /auth/check reports authentication state without tokens.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(12. Session architecture) Tj T*
(request_context.py stores a ContextVar request key. mcp_session_middleware.py binds each MCP) Tj T*
(request to its connection session ID. session_store.py stores AuthSession objects by key.) Tj T*
(auth_session.py reads and writes the session associated with the current key. Stateful MCP) Tj T*
(connections are isolated by connection key. Known limitation: stateless HTTP has no stable MCP) Tj T*
(session ID and currently falls back to the shared stdio key. Stateless multi-user deployment) Tj T*
(is therefore unsafe and requires a future fix. This project does not claim that fix is) Tj T*
(implemented.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(13. Tenant isolation and authorization) Tj T*
(Tenant ID comes from the authenticated PointNXT response or controlled development) Tj T*
(configuration. It is stored with AuthSession and propagated as x-tenant-id. No MCP tool) Tj T*
(accepts tenantId, so the model cannot directly choose another tenant. The MCP does not) Tj T*
(implement RBAC, membership checks, role checks, or admin checks. Authorization is delegated to) Tj T*
(PointNXT backend controls.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(14. Shared API client) Tj T*
(PointNXTAPI supports synchronous and asynchronous GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE. Read tools use) Tj T*
(async GET. Requests use JSON headers, bearer authentication, tenant propagation, request IDs,) Tj T*
(latency metrics, structured logs, timeout handling, and retries for) Tj T*
(timeout/connection/502/503/504. A 401 performs one refresh and retries once. PII-like) Tj T*
(parameter values, including generic search, are fingerprinted before logging. Tokens and) Tj T*
(passwords are not logged.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(15. Validation) Tj T*
(services/validation.py provides page_limit with maximum 100, optional_text with maximum 200) Tj T*
(characters, optional_id, and optional_date. Orders and products also retain domain validation.) Tj T*
(Customer, shipment, return, and business tools use shared validators. Status validation is) Tj T*
(domain-specific. Boolean values are rejected for numeric pagination where the validator is) Tj T*
(applied.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(16. Errors and security) Tj T*
(The client normalizes timeout, connection, HTTP, refresh, and validation failures. No-result) Tj T*
(responses are explicit. Customer ambiguity returns candidates. Business composite tools return) Tj T*
(successful sections and unavailable entries with safe error codes: backend_unavailable,) Tj T*
(authentication_required, request_timeout, and section_failed. Request logs retain timestamp,) Tj T*
(request ID, method, endpoint, status, attempts, latency, and tenant metadata while) Tj T*
(fingerprinting sensitive parameters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(17. Tests) Tj T*
(test_orders.py covers order validation, retrieval, summaries, stats, transitions, and) Tj T*
(failures. test_customers.py covers deduplication, context, and ambiguity. test_products.py) Tj T*
(covers filters, pagination, lookup, summary, and default pagination. test_inventory.py covers) Tj T*
(inventory views and summaries. test_shipments.py covers stored shipment and fulfillment) Tj T*
(limitations. test_returns.py covers return statuses/items and refund non-execution.) Tj T*
(test_business.py covers business summary and attention behavior. test_security.py covers) Tj T*
(session/tenant helper isolation, safe logging parameters, partial failures, and registered) Tj T*
(tool names.) Tj T*
(Remaining test gaps include full stateful HTTP integration, safe stateless HTTP behavior,) Tj T*
(backend RBAC, real backend contract tests, and end-to-end browser callback testing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
