(18. Deployment) Tj T*
(Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml run the server on port 8000. Configuration comes from .env:) Tj T*
(POINTNXT_BASE_URL, POINTNXT_LOGIN_URL, POINTNXT_AUTH_CALLBACK_URL, POINTNXT_ACCESS_TOKEN,) Tj T*
(POINTNXT_REFRESH_TOKEN, POINTNXT_REFRESH_ENDPOINT, POINTNXT_TENANT_ID, DEV_MODE, and) Tj T*
(AUTH_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT. The documented HTTP startup is server.mcp.run\('streamable-http',) Tj T*
(host='0.0.0.0', port=8000\). External URL and proxy configuration are not fixed by source code.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(19. Current limitations and readiness) Tj T*
(Implemented: read-only order/product querying, derived customer/shipment/return views, backend) Tj T*
(inventory summaries, authentication and refresh, tenant header propagation, diagnostics,) Tj T*
(compact business tools, validation, safe parameter logging, tests, and Docker deployment.) Tj T*
(Partially implemented/backend-dependent: customer data, shipment detail, returns,) Tj T*
(inspection/putaway, stock semantics, analytics, authorization.) Tj T*
(Not implemented: commerce mutations, dedicated customer/inventory/shipment/return/refund APIs,) Tj T*
(RBAC, live tracking refresh, arbitrary priority ranking.) Tj T*
(Ready for controlled office testing with trusted users and stateful sessions. Stateful multi-) Tj T*
(user production still needs end-to-end transport isolation tests and backend authorization) Tj T*
(confirmation. Stateless multi-user deployment is not ready because of the shared fallback) Tj T*
(session key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(20. Design decisions) Tj T*
(Existing backend services are reused to avoid duplicate business logic. Customer, shipment,) Tj T*
(and return features are derived from orders because dedicated APIs are not confirmed.) Tj T*
(Inventory is not calculated locally because backend semantics must control sellable stock. Raw) Tj T*
(and compact tools coexist for backward compatibility. Write tools were intentionally not) Tj T*
(added. tenantId is kept out of MCP parameters to prevent model-controlled tenant switching.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(21. Example interactions) Tj T*
(Find order #1503: search_orders\(order_reference='1503'\), then) Tj T*
(get_order\(order_reference='#1503'\) for detail. Find Krishna Saraf: find_customer\(name='Krishna) Tj T*
(Saraf'\), then get_customer_context with a unique candidate. Products matching Laptop:) Tj T*
(search_products\(name='Laptop'\). Track order: get_order_shipments\(order_reference='#1503'\),) Tj T*
(which reports stored data only. Returns: get_order_returns\(order_reference='#1503'\). Daily) Tj T*
(summary: get_business_summary\(\). Attention: get_attention_queue\(\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(22. Quick reference) Tj T*
(Important files: server.py; tools/orders.py, customers.py, products.py, shipments.py,) Tj T*
(returns.py, business.py, auth.py; services/pointnxt_api.py, auth_session.py, session_store.py,) Tj T*
(request_context.py, mcp_session_middleware.py, validation.py, metrics.py. Confirmed endpoints) Tj T*
(are auth login/logout/refresh plus commerce orders/products and their stats/summary/status) Tj T*
(metadata. Main risks are stateless HTTP session fallback, backend-dependent authorization, and) Tj T*
(missing dedicated domain APIs.) Tj T*
ET
